5417 true] [17592186412804 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412794 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412795 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412797 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412799 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1075 #edb/ref 17592186412801 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1077 "selection" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1078 #edb/ref 17592186412799 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412804 1079 #uuid "6f7e02fc-389b-5a53-ab92-9e7d664ea877" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412805 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412804 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412805 1069 "q-330333" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412805 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412805 1071 "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)\\times {x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)=-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412805 1072 #uuid "71a6807f-51a3-5e94-a65a-0087aa5dc119" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412805 1074 "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a scalar multiple of any of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multiplier is not a constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n-3\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=0$ and ${c}_{2}=-3,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412806 1068 #edb/ref 17592186412803 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412806 1069 "q-330354" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412806 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412806 1071 "Suppose ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are both solutions of the homogeneous system\n${x}^{′}(t)=A\\text{ }x(t).$\nWhich of the following is **always** a solution of the same system?\n\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{1}(t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot {x}_{2}(t)$\n- $x(t)={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)$" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412806 1072 #uuid "e5a0af42-71ea-5bb3-8eb8-b8b29ef8a2c6" 13194139534166 17592186045417 true] [17592186412806 1074 "The *linearity principle* for systems of linear ordinary differential equations (ODEs) states that if ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are solutions to a homogeneous linear system, then for any constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2},$ the linear combination \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis also a solution of the system. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given expressions.\n\n- Option I is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1,$ respectively.\n\n- Option II might be *not* a solution to the system since it's not a linear combination of the solutions ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t).$ Notice that the multipliers of the first and the second terms are not constant.\n\n- Option III is a solution to the system. Indeed, notice that\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\n$$\n\nis a linear combination of the solutions with constant multiplies ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=-1,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139534166 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-072d3215-6073-5918-a9fe-1dcc32903f2d" 17592186412793 "answer-892c08a4-3464-5326-833d-0cac32b879f0" 17592186412794 "answer-8cfbf6a0-2987-5862-8e6d-5405fa26152f" 17592186412795 "answer-b96cdf9a-49a4-54e5-9dfc-848510bf8222" 17592186412796 "answer-cd9aacf5-3935-547f-8a01-96b4e4f8e273" 17592186412797 "answer-cf25f748-5f77-5753-848b-d0fd49da67dc" 17592186412798 "answer-d51c3cc8-7840-5e1e-8a53-1bf6714d0841" 17592186412799 "answer-e0c4b1ce-27b0-544b-a5c2-9c96a3531721" 17592186412800 "answer-e8a1cc24-066e-5fd9-aec3-63dcebd27b5a" 17592186412801 "answer-eae566d9-a61e-5385-975a-ff789b6dc62b" 17592186412802 "answer-field-1f03c56a-d1c9-5e79-89bf-0c51f2598a8f" 17592186412803 "answer-field-6f7e02fc-389b-5a53-ab92-9e7d664ea877" 17592186412804 "question-71a6807f-51a3-5e94-a65a-0087aa5dc119" 17592186412805 "question-e5a0af42-71ea-5bb3-8eb8-b8b29ef8a2c6" 17592186412806}}
